      "content": "Based on the descriptions provided, for a high-level boardroom environment, I would rank Candidate A, James Whitmont, as the top choice. His extensive experience in international stakeholder management and background from the Wharton School, along with his previous position at Goldman Sachs - a firm known for its stakes in leadership profiles - suggests he would immediately \"command the room.\" His polished experience is paramount when presenting directly to Fortune 500 boards, indicating a strong \"executive presence\" and a good \"cultural fit.\"",
